HANDLING EMPTY QUERY RESULTS
============================
If a catalog query returns blank:
1. Verify the connected DB2 database.
2. Verify the exact schema name and case.
3. Verify the catalog view and column names for the installed DB2 LUW version.
4. Verify metadata permissions.
5. Run a simple count query using the same schema filter.
6. Check whether an object is defined in another schema or references an object in another schema.
7. Record "verified absent" only after the query and scope are validated.

